WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.600 --> 00:00:03.269
GRADY: Here in the forge,
it's all about the blades.

00:00:03.369 --> 00:00:07.207
But tonight we've got the
ultimate forging smackdown.

00:00:07.307 --> 00:00:09.775
This is our first
ever WWE challenge.

00:00:09.842 --> 00:00:11.343
 Woo!

00:00:11.410 --> 00:00:13.880
GRADY: Only one smith will
claim victory and a WWE title

00:00:13.947 --> 00:00:17.417
from the legend, Nature
Boy himself, Ric Flair.

00:00:22.122 --> 00:00:23.122
[music playing]

00:00:23.188 --> 00:00:24.623
Hunter, Phil, congratulations.

00:00:24.690 --> 00:00:26.993
The two of you have beat out
the competition, which means

00:00:27.059 --> 00:00:28.494
you're moving into round three.

00:00:28.561 --> 00:00:31.230
Now, with the Forged in
Fire title, $10,000 check,

00:00:31.330 --> 00:00:34.401
and the WWE title on
the line, this challenge

00:00:34.467 --> 00:00:35.501
is far from over.

00:00:35.601 --> 00:00:37.103
In this last round,
we're going to send you

00:00:37.203 --> 00:00:39.505
back to your home forges
to build a wicked warrior's

00:00:39.572 --> 00:00:40.273
weapon from history.

00:00:40.340 --> 00:00:41.340
You guys ready to rumble?

00:00:41.407 --> 00:00:42.174
 Oh, yeah.

00:00:42.241 --> 00:00:43.476
- Ready.
- All right, gentlemen.

00:00:43.543 --> 00:00:44.644
You guys are going
to be building this.

00:00:47.112 --> 00:00:49.849
The bastard sword.

00:00:49.915 --> 00:00:51.216
NARRATOR: The bastard
sword was widely

00:00:51.317 --> 00:00:53.152
popular throughout Europe,
during the Middle Ages,

00:00:53.218 --> 00:00:54.687
and well into the Renaissance.

00:00:54.754 --> 00:00:57.123
It's so well-known, a
version of this deadly blade

00:00:57.190 --> 00:01:00.592
was wielded by the famous
bastard Jon Snow in HBO's "Game

00:01:00.659 --> 00:01:01.995
of Thrones."

00:01:02.095 --> 00:01:04.831
While its blade length
varied from 36 to 40 inches,

00:01:04.931 --> 00:01:08.401
the name came from its uniquely
sized handle that was between

00:01:08.467 --> 00:01:11.538
one and two hands long, earning
it its alternative name,

00:01:11.638 --> 00:01:12.872
the hand-and-a-half sword.

00:01:12.939 --> 00:01:14.974
Lethal in battle, the
sword could easily

00:01:15.040 --> 00:01:16.943
deliver devastating
blows with two hands,

00:01:17.010 --> 00:01:20.580
or quickly inflict slashes in
close-quarters combat with one.

00:01:20.680 --> 00:01:22.648
 So, gentlemen, you got four
days in your home forges.

00:01:22.715 --> 00:01:23.516
Good luck.

00:01:23.616 --> 00:01:24.184
We'll see you then.

00:01:24.284 --> 00:01:25.484 line:14%
 Good luck, brother.

00:01:25.585 --> 00:01:27.220 line:14%
[music playing]

00:01:27.286 --> 00:01:30.122 line:8%
I am Hunter The Vulcan
Viking Copeland,

00:01:30.222 --> 00:01:31.657
from Broken Arrow, Oklahoma.

00:01:31.724 --> 00:01:34.827
Vulcan is the blacksmith who
forged all of the weapons

00:01:34.894 --> 00:01:36.195
for the Greek gods.

00:01:36.296 --> 00:01:38.464
So, you know, I got a
little Viking style here,

00:01:38.565 --> 00:01:40.766
and I got a little Vulcan
blood, so that's where

00:01:40.833 --> 00:01:42.201
I'm getting my skills today.

00:01:42.268 --> 00:01:45.704
Now, I am stoked to be here
on the WWE competition.

00:01:45.804 --> 00:01:47.006
I want this piece to look good.

00:01:47.072 --> 00:01:48.941
So my finger just wraps
around right there.

00:01:49.008 --> 00:01:49.909
Nice and comfy.

00:01:50.009 --> 00:01:50.909
I like it.

00:01:50.976 --> 00:01:51.744
The blade blade is quenched.

00:01:51.811 --> 00:01:52.812
I feel great.

00:01:52.878 --> 00:01:54.213
I'm a little ahead of schedule.

00:01:54.313 --> 00:01:56.549
I have a little extra time
right now, so I'm deciding

00:01:56.616 --> 00:01:57.784 line:14%
to temper on the clock--

00:01:57.884 --> 00:01:59.218 line:14%
 Yes, sir!

00:01:59.318 --> 00:02:00.586 line:8%
--which pulls some of the
hardness out of the blade

00:02:00.686 --> 00:02:03.356
and gives it the
flexibility and the strength

00:02:03.422 --> 00:02:06.425
that it needs to put up with J.

00:02:06.492 --> 00:02:07.393
 Oof.

00:02:07.493 --> 00:02:08.628
HUNTER (VOICEOVER):
My blade's getting

00:02:08.695 --> 00:02:09.228
too hot in this one area.

00:02:09.328 --> 00:02:10.429
It spells trouble.

00:02:10.529 --> 00:02:12.098
 This is the thinnest
part of the blade.

00:02:12.164 --> 00:02:13.065
I should have thought of that.

00:02:13.165 --> 00:02:14.734
Let's see what happens.

00:02:14.834 --> 00:02:17.236
HUNTER: So here we go,
putting the handle together.

00:02:17.302 --> 00:02:19.639
The epoxy sets, but
I've started to notice

00:02:19.739 --> 00:02:23.042
that I have a large gap right
here underneath the guard.

00:02:23.142 --> 00:02:24.343
This is bad.

00:02:24.443 --> 00:02:25.778
I just want it to not
come loose and start

00:02:25.844 --> 00:02:27.547
jingling around in their hand.

00:02:27.614 --> 00:02:29.448
 See what I can do.

00:02:29.515 --> 00:02:32.919
HUNTER: I'm going to kind
of wrap wire nice and tight,

00:02:33.019 --> 00:02:35.387
all in there, and epoxy
it down into place

00:02:35.488 --> 00:02:38.291
and just kind of hide this
little mistake I have.

00:02:38.358 --> 00:02:39.658
 Oh, that's perfect.

00:02:39.759 --> 00:02:41.060
HUNTE: It doesn't look
the way I wish it looked,

00:02:41.126 --> 00:02:43.096
but it's really not that bad.

00:02:43.163 --> 00:02:44.731
I'm not going to let these
guys have all the fun,

00:02:44.797 --> 00:02:49.602
so I'm going to do a
little bit of testing.

00:02:49.669 --> 00:02:52.104
 [roars] Yeah!

00:02:52.205 --> 00:02:55.175 line:14%
[music playing]

00:02:56.509 --> 00:02:59.078 line:8%
PHIL: My name is Phil, but they
call me Sergeant Cheesebadger.

00:02:59.178 --> 00:03:01.381 line:8%
I'm from Wisconsin,
I'm a former Marine,

00:03:01.481 --> 00:03:03.382
and I'm here to take
home the victory.

00:03:03.449 --> 00:03:05.851
I'm not dropping a flying
elbow off the top ropes,

00:03:05.951 --> 00:03:10.022
but I'm just going to try to
make the sickest blade I can.

00:03:10.089 --> 00:03:11.724
 Almost halfway there.

00:03:11.791 --> 00:03:14.827
PHIL: And the billet is
solid, so I'm feeling

00:03:14.894 --> 00:03:16.028
pretty confident about it.

00:03:16.128 --> 00:03:17.263
 All right.

00:03:17.363 --> 00:03:19.264
I got the profile
right where I want,

00:03:19.364 --> 00:03:22.601
and I'm getting ready
to quench my blade.

00:03:22.668 --> 00:03:24.036
PHIL (VOICEOVER):
Anything could happen

00:03:24.103 --> 00:03:25.337
when you go in to quench.

00:03:25.404 --> 00:03:28.240
It could crack or bend
or warp, and I really

00:03:28.307 --> 00:03:29.475
don't want that to happen.

00:03:29.542 --> 00:03:32.678
It's time to go
in for the quench.

00:03:32.778 --> 00:03:33.912
I don't hear any pings.

00:03:33.979 --> 00:03:35.147
I don't hear any tings.

00:03:35.214 --> 00:03:36.048
 All right.

00:03:36.115 --> 00:03:37.750
Everything looks great.

00:03:37.817 --> 00:03:39.418
We might have a good sword.

00:03:39.485 --> 00:03:41.687
PHIL: I have enough here
to grind a straight blade,

00:03:41.787 --> 00:03:43.289
which is awesome.

00:03:43.356 --> 00:03:46.659
 Mild steel is so soft, it
almost just drills like wood.

00:03:46.726 --> 00:03:47.827
Look at that.

00:03:47.927 --> 00:03:49.228
PHIL: So I'm going through
my tap and die set,

00:03:49.294 --> 00:03:50.863
and I'm realizing
that the smallest

00:03:50.963 --> 00:03:52.365
set that I have is 1/4 inch.

00:03:52.431 --> 00:03:54.634
And my tang is nowhere
near that wide.

00:03:56.836 --> 00:03:58.904
PHIL: If I had five
more hours, I would

00:03:58.971 --> 00:04:00.339
definitely thread that tang.

00:04:00.406 --> 00:04:02.375
It's just a tighter
construction.

00:04:02.475 --> 00:04:05.945
But I need to move on, so
I'm going with the peening,

00:04:06.011 --> 00:04:07.347
because I'm running out of time.

00:04:09.849 --> 00:04:11.650
PHIL (VOICEOVER): Hopefully,
it all stays tight.

00:04:11.751 --> 00:04:14.287
 That should do.

00:04:14.354 --> 00:04:17.857
[music playing]

00:04:19.225 --> 00:04:20.727
 Well, bladesmiths,
welcome back to the forge.

00:04:20.793 --> 00:04:25.164
Guys, I got to say your
bastard swords look fantastic.

00:04:25.230 --> 00:04:26.599
We're going to get into them.

00:04:26.666 --> 00:04:29.435
But first, I got a special
guest I gotta introduce.

00:04:29.502 --> 00:04:33.072
Please join me in welcoming
an absolute legend, a WWE

00:04:33.172 --> 00:04:35.675
Hall of Famer, and one of the
most prolific, and I'd say,

00:04:35.741 --> 00:04:40.246
the most stylish WWE superstar
of all time, Nature Boy,

00:04:40.313 --> 00:04:41.681
Ric Flair.

00:04:41.747 --> 00:04:47.387
ANNOUNCER: Heavyweight
champion, Nature Boy, Ric Flair!

00:04:50.122 --> 00:04:51.457
[applause]

00:04:51.524 --> 00:04:52.058
 Woo!

00:04:54.927 --> 00:04:55.727
You guys ready to play?

00:04:55.794 --> 00:04:56.429
 Yeah.

00:04:56.529 --> 00:04:56.962
 Always.

00:04:57.062 --> 00:04:58.364
 Ready.

00:04:58.431 --> 00:05:02.868
 There's $10,000 on the
line, plus an opportunity

00:05:02.935 --> 00:05:04.270
to carry the big gold.

00:05:04.336 --> 00:05:06.138
I don't know how cool
that is to you guys.

00:05:06.205 --> 00:05:08.574
It's very cool to me.

00:05:08.674 --> 00:05:10.709
 Pssh.

00:05:10.810 --> 00:05:12.077
This is crazy!

00:05:12.144 --> 00:05:13.579
 Dave, are you ready, man?

00:05:13.646 --> 00:05:14.112
 Good to go.

00:05:14.213 --> 00:05:14.981
 Let's do this.

00:05:19.351 --> 00:05:20.186
 All right, gentlemen.

00:05:20.286 --> 00:05:21.220
You know what time it is.

00:05:21.320 --> 00:05:23.022
It's time for the kill test.

00:05:23.088 --> 00:05:24.223
I'm going to take your swords.

00:05:24.323 --> 00:05:26.458
I'm going to attack
this gel torso here.

00:05:26.558 --> 00:05:28.961
See what kind of damage we do.

00:05:29.062 --> 00:05:30.162
Hunter, you're up first.
You ready?

00:05:30.229 --> 00:05:30.963
 Yes, sir.

00:05:31.030 --> 00:05:32.998
DAVE: OK.

00:05:33.065 --> 00:05:34.567
HUNTER: Oh, I'm just stoked.

00:05:34.667 --> 00:05:36.769
It is the lifelong dream of
a bladesmith to make a sword

00:05:36.869 --> 00:05:38.671
and whack one of those
ballistic dummies.

00:05:38.738 --> 00:05:40.138
I'm just going to
be lopping limbs

00:05:40.205 --> 00:05:41.173
or something off this thing.

00:05:41.239 --> 00:05:44.310
I'm so excited for this moment.

00:05:44.377 --> 00:05:46.878
 Come on, baby.

00:05:46.979 --> 00:05:50.316
[hardcore music]

00:05:50.383 --> 00:05:54.620
[grunting]

00:06:01.260 --> 00:06:02.728
RIC FLAIR: Woo!

00:06:02.795 --> 00:06:03.896
Very cool, man.

00:06:06.665 --> 00:06:07.900
DAVE: Yeah, I think he's done.

00:06:11.570 --> 00:06:12.437
All right, Hunter.

00:06:12.504 --> 00:06:13.773
Right off, it's a performer.

00:06:13.873 --> 00:06:15.841
It cut deep on each
one of those cuts.

00:06:15.908 --> 00:06:18.344
As a matter of fact, that one
downward diagonal goes all

00:06:18.410 --> 00:06:19.678
the way through the rib cage.

00:06:19.779 --> 00:06:21.313
Handle could have been
just a little bit longer.

00:06:21.413 --> 00:06:22.949
I'm winding up with about
a hand and a quarter

00:06:23.015 --> 00:06:24.350
instead of a hand and a half.

00:06:24.416 --> 00:06:26.318
But you definitely got
a lethal blade here.

00:06:26.385 --> 00:06:27.453
 Thank you.

00:06:27.553 --> 00:06:28.887
DAVE: All right,
Phillip, you're up.

00:06:28.954 --> 00:06:29.555
You ready?

00:06:29.622 --> 00:06:30.456
 Ready.

00:06:32.825 --> 00:06:35.160
[energetic music]

00:06:35.227 --> 00:06:38.798
[grunting]

00:06:53.446 --> 00:06:55.180
 Oh, my gosh.

00:06:55.280 --> 00:06:56.248
 Very cool.

00:06:56.315 --> 00:06:57.616
Very cool.

00:06:57.683 --> 00:06:59.919
DAVE: So right off, I like
the scale of your blade.

00:06:59.985 --> 00:07:03.022
I mean, it's very large, and
it's got a lot of weight to it,

00:07:03.122 --> 00:07:04.556
but the balance is nice.

00:07:04.623 --> 00:07:06.425
You can see all these
cuts are so deep,

00:07:06.491 --> 00:07:07.927
I was actually worried
on that last one

00:07:08.027 --> 00:07:10.762
that I would hit the post
that's holding that thing up.

00:07:10.862 --> 00:07:15.267
But as far as being a cutting
sword, this thing is lethal.

00:07:15.334 --> 00:07:16.068
Good job.

00:07:16.168 --> 00:07:16.969
 Thank you.

00:07:20.439 --> 00:07:21.407
 You having fun doing this?

00:07:21.474 --> 00:07:22.208
 Oh, yeah.

00:07:22.275 --> 00:07:23.209
 Making history?

00:07:23.276 --> 00:07:24.109
 Feeling good.

00:07:24.176 --> 00:07:25.144
 So what's up next?

00:07:25.244 --> 00:07:26.445
You ready for this?

00:07:26.512 --> 00:07:29.749
We're going to test the
strength of your swords.

00:07:29.816 --> 00:07:30.349
You ready, J?

00:07:30.416 --> 00:07:31.283
 Oh, yeah.

00:07:31.350 --> 00:07:32.218
RIC FLAIR: Very cool.

00:07:32.284 --> 00:07:33.119
J: Thank you, sir.

00:07:36.956 --> 00:07:38.423
[music playing]

00:07:38.490 --> 00:07:39.892
Bladesmiths, welcome
to our strength

00:07:39.959 --> 00:07:43.929
test, the WWE Bashfest.

00:07:43.996 --> 00:07:47.400
To test the edge holding ability
and overall construction,

00:07:47.500 --> 00:07:50.636
I'm going to go through
a series of WWE weapons.

00:07:50.702 --> 00:07:52.772
We're going to destroy
the table, puncture

00:07:52.872 --> 00:07:54.607
and bash through
the garbage can,

00:07:54.673 --> 00:07:57.343
and just tear that
ladder to pieces.

00:07:57.409 --> 00:07:58.644
Hunter, you're up first.
You ready to go?

00:07:58.744 --> 00:07:59.712
 Yes, sir.
J: All right.

00:07:59.812 --> 00:08:00.613
Let's do it.

00:08:02.848 --> 00:08:05.084
 J, steal the show, brother.

00:08:07.920 --> 00:08:09.154
 [grunts]

00:08:09.254 --> 00:08:09.888
 Damn.

00:08:09.989 --> 00:08:13.626
[music playing]

00:08:16.061 --> 00:08:20.032
[grunting]

00:08:33.012 --> 00:08:35.181
 Oh, man.

00:08:35.281 --> 00:08:36.649
 Hunter, you started
out strong, man.

00:08:36.749 --> 00:08:37.683
 Ugh.

00:08:37.783 --> 00:08:39.018
 This is actually
very comfortable,

00:08:39.084 --> 00:08:40.585
even though the handle's
a little bit short.

00:08:40.652 --> 00:08:42.988
But you look at the grain--

00:08:43.055 --> 00:08:43.789
it looks like sand.

00:08:43.889 --> 00:08:44.890
 Mm-hmm.

00:08:44.956 --> 00:08:46.158
J: So that caused a weak
point, and the shock

00:08:46.258 --> 00:08:47.259
wave went all the way down.

00:08:47.326 --> 00:08:49.294
It snapped it at
this weak point.

00:08:49.394 --> 00:08:50.429
Sorry, man.

00:08:50.496 --> 00:08:51.264
 My heart.

00:08:55.701 --> 00:08:57.269
 Hunter, it's
painful to see, man.

00:08:57.336 --> 00:08:59.705
You put a lot of work into
that thing, and it looks great.

00:08:59.772 --> 00:09:01.907
But unfortunately, you did
have a catastrophic failure

00:09:01.974 --> 00:09:03.475
on the ladder, which
means you can't

00:09:03.542 --> 00:09:04.877
test your blade any further.

00:09:04.977 --> 00:09:06.712
But you are not out
of the fight yet.

00:09:06.812 --> 00:09:08.580
Philip, in order
to claim the title,

00:09:08.680 --> 00:09:10.182
you've got to make
it through the table.

00:09:10.282 --> 00:09:12.952
You've got to make it through
all the swings to the trashcan,

00:09:13.018 --> 00:09:15.521
and you've got to make it
through at least one bash

00:09:15.588 --> 00:09:16.656
into the ladder.

00:09:16.756 --> 00:09:18.457
You prepared for it?

00:09:18.557 --> 00:09:20.693
 I'm nervous, but I'm ready.

00:09:20.793 --> 00:09:21.994
 Woo!

00:09:22.061 --> 00:09:23.796
Get in the spirit, man?

00:09:23.863 --> 00:09:24.763
 [laughs]

00:09:24.830 --> 00:09:26.332
 Let's see what
your blade can do.

00:09:26.398 --> 00:09:28.534
J?

00:09:28.601 --> 00:09:32.238
[music playing]

00:09:34.040 --> 00:09:34.807
 (WHISPERING) Damn.

00:09:42.147 --> 00:09:46.118
[grunting]

00:09:51.123 --> 00:09:52.091
 Well done.

00:09:56.128 --> 00:09:58.196
GRADY: Hunter, man,
you fought hard.

00:09:58.296 --> 00:09:59.865
The first rounds, you excelled.

00:09:59.965 --> 00:10:01.400
But unfortunately,
during the testing,

00:10:01.500 --> 00:10:04.170
you did suffer catastrophic
failure, and for that reason,

00:10:04.270 --> 00:10:05.404
your time in the
forge has ended.

00:10:05.504 --> 00:10:06.605
I'm going to have
to ask you to please

00:10:06.705 --> 00:10:09.174
step off the forge floor, bud.

00:10:09.241 --> 00:10:10.442
PHIL: Thank you, Hunter.

00:10:10.509 --> 00:10:11.610
 Thank you guys.

00:10:11.677 --> 00:10:12.978
Thank you very much.

00:10:13.079 --> 00:10:14.413
GRADY: Well, Philip, you
know what that means, man.

00:10:14.513 --> 00:10:16.481
You are the "Forged
in Fire" champion.

00:10:16.548 --> 00:10:18.851
RIC FLAIR: Philip,
congratulations, man!

00:10:18.951 --> 00:10:20.453
Woo!

00:10:20.519 --> 00:10:22.721
GRADY: That comes with
a check for $10,000,

00:10:22.788 --> 00:10:26.224
as well as a WWE title.

00:10:26.324 --> 00:10:27.192
 Here we go, man.

00:10:27.259 --> 00:10:28.060
[laughter]

00:10:28.160 --> 00:10:28.894
 Get that 10 grand.

00:10:28.994 --> 00:10:30.462
 Get out of this man's way!

00:10:30.529 --> 00:10:31.663
 Woo!

00:10:31.763 --> 00:10:34.766
PHIL: "Forged in Fire"
champion, brother!

00:10:34.866 --> 00:10:38.737
This title is going in the most
obnoxious spot of the living

00:10:38.804 --> 00:10:40.172
room that I can find.

00:10:40.239 --> 00:10:43.142
Probably taped onto the TV.

00:10:43.209 --> 00:10:45.010
 Let me hear it one time.

00:10:45.077 --> 00:10:46.144
BOTH: Woo!

00:10:46.211 --> 00:10:47.546
 [laughs]

00:10:47.613 --> 00:10:51.117
[music playing]

